WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.252
Module 2 builds directly on this foundation.

00:00:03.252 --> 00:00:10.367
Now that we can talk about data meaning and quality, we will design relational structures that preserve that

00:00:10.367 --> 00:00:16.332
meaning. You will define row grain, identify entities and attributes, choose keys,

00:00:16.332 --> 00:00:21.872
connect tables through relationships, and use constraints to protect important rules.

00:00:21.872 --> 00:00:29.532
The same habit continues: define the concept first, then choose the technical representation that supports it.

00:00:29.532 --> 00:00:33.852
As you move forward, keep the reasoning habits from this module.

00:00:33.852 --> 00:00:39.617
The next topic will add new SQL tools, but it still depends on understanding grain, missing values,

00:00:39.617 --> 00:00:42.942
and the meaning of each transformation.
